  "evidence": {
    "R1184": "Original GetPIFConfigFiles call discards void return; actual MSVC x86 object sections/relocations unchanged without added nt_pif.h. C4013 alone is not failure.",
    "R1185": "lim_page_frame_init original return is IBOOL=int and ignored by caller; no ABI difference without prototype; remove prototype/comments. Firmware binding and layered registry header remain necessary: native SystemDirectory is modern OS, and native registry ignores approved NTVDM.REG overlay. Residual headers remain pending, not justified by circular include dependency.",
    "R1186": "PCHAR versus host_addr casts have same native pointer representation at selected sas_loads ABI; declaration/cast control32 object sections equal. Restore PCHAR.",
    "R1187": "Comment described host-ISA confusion, but actual supported commands leave i386 undefined. Original outer !i386 already selects software CPU; comment removed.",
    "R1188": "Restore original MIPS_BIT_MASK statement and remove redundant project CPU_40_STYLE inner selector. No selection or value change in actual supported CCPU build.",
    "R1189": "Original i386 hardware body is already excluded by#error. Keep original outer branch framework and#error; no hardware code restored. Point retires as no remaining selected-code deviation.",
    "R1190": "Remove locally added redundant nested selector closure; preserve original i386 boundary and#line128.",
    "R1191": "Restore original GetSystemDirectory-shaped directory retrieval, error text, CreateFile/size/read/SAS flow. NtvdmGetSystemDirectoryA supplies selected immutable installation system32, not modern host system32. Keep suffix-inclusive capacity check to retain previous helper bounded-write contract. No new adapter.",
    "R1192": "TerminateVDM->terminate->host_terminate->ExitProcess never returns on selected product path; repeated termination also calls exit. Remove added unreachable return(-1).",
    "R1193": "Original strcat(buffer,\"\\ntio.sys\") restored after bounded selected-directory retrieval; CreateFile owns missing-file result again.",
    "R1194": "Original nt_pif.c GetPIFConfigFiles documents MAX_PATH+8.3 and calls ExpandEnvironmentStringsOem with MAX_PATH+12. Original MAX_PATH caller cannot hold all allowed output. Keep +12, remove comment; no new storage/state.",
    "R1195": "Read-only admitted VirtualDeviceDrivers key is absent in current host (Test-Path false). Absence is supported no-VDD installation, not corrupt NT4 setup. Preserve omission of installation-error popup; restore original RegOpenKeyEx layout and KEY_QUERY_VALUE. Facade explicitly ignores access and delegates same read-only projection; downstream query failures unchanged. Scope: current omission still suppresses every open-failure dialog, preserving pre-batch behavior. Evidence requires no dialog for missing optional key only, not allocation/access failures. Narrowing suppression to ERROR_FILE_NOT_FOUND would require extra result capture/condition and net-increase versus the minimized one-line omission; this is an explicit owner decision, not a claimed universal necessity."
